\title{Gather, scatter, expanding load and compressing store}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-15}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{language}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1004}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|simd::gather~} and \code{\verb~|simd::scatter~} read and write lane i at the element given by lane i of an index vector, counted from a base pointer. \code{\verb~|simd::load_expand~} places consecutive elements of memory in the set lanes of a mask, and \code{\verb~|simd::store_compress~} writes the set lanes consecutively, which packs what a filter keeps. All four take one-dimensional vectors of numbers. See [memory](design-simd-vectors-memory). \pr{1004}.}
